# The stem's files this node carries MODIFIED, each with the reason it differs.
#
# This is template-commit-reveal's `upstream/with/indexer`: a ROOT of this repo
# fed from jolly-roger `with/indexer` (`"stemBranch": "with/indexer"`), which
# holds jolly-roger's branch exactly, so that `with/indexer` here can merge it
# beside `main` (a branch has in-repo stems or one cross-repo stem, never both;
# plan F1b, decision F1-2, on jolly-roger `work`). It modifies none of the
# stem's files, which is what the empty section below says, and it is checked
# like every list, by `scripts/check-divergences.mjs` (run by
# `web/test/offshoot-divergences.test.ts`).
#
# WHY THIS FILE IS THIS REPO'S AND NOT JOLLY-ROGER'S, the one file of this node
# that is not the stem's. A child repo's list is its own. jolly-roger's ends in
# a `[with/indexer]` section, and the check takes a list's last marker as the
# node it describes: here that would name THIS repo's `with/indexer`, whose
# stems include this branch, so the check compared the node with itself and
# failed. On a cascade from jolly-roger that conflicts on this file, keep this
# side, always.
#
# FORMAT. One file per line: its path, then its reason. `#` starts a comment.
# A line `[<branch>]` starts a section.

[upstream/with/indexer]
